## Usage

```python
import torch
from transformers import AutoModelForSequenceClassification, AutoTokenizer

repo = "{{ repo_id }}"
tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(repo{% if not m.shipped %}, revision="{{ m.branch }}"{% endif %})
model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(repo{% if not m.shipped %}, revision="{{ m.branch }}"{% endif %}).eval()
text = "{{ m.query_prefix }}" + "where is my shipment?"   # the E5 prefix is required
with torch.no_grad():
    logits = model(**tok(text, return_tensors="pt", truncation=True, max_length={{ m.max_length }})).logits
print(model.config.id2label[int(logits.argmax(-1))])
```

Abstention (the out-of-distribution flag) is NOT part of the plain model: it needs `predict.py` and `ood_bank.safetensors` from the same repository, used as follows. Confidences are temperature-scaled (T = {{ m.temperature | f4 }}); messages whose Mahalanobis score falls below the threshold ({{ thresholds.v1 | f2 }} v1 / {{ thresholds.v3 | f2 }} v3; this model's threshold = {{ m.ood_threshold | f2 }}, set to retain {{ m.retention | pct }}% of validation rows) are flagged `abstained`.

```python
from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download
import sys
path = snapshot_download("{{ repo_id }}", revision="{{ m.branch }}"){% if not publish %}  # private repo: needs an authorised token{% endif %}
sys.path.insert(0, path)
from predict import IntentRouter          # needs only torch, transformers, safetensors, numpy
router = IntentRouter.from_pretrained(path)
router.predict("...")   # {label, confidence, ood_score, abstained, top3}
```

## Training data

A {{ eda.n_rows }}-row synthetic logistics intent dataset ({{ eda.n_classes }} classes, per-class counts {{ eda.min_class }} to {{ eda.max_class }}) provided for an assessment. It is **not redistributed** and no dataset text is included. Fixed splits: {{ m.n_train }} training rows, {{ m.n_val }} validation rows (epoch, temperature and threshold selection), {{ m.test.n }} test rows (one logged evaluation); model seed {{ m.model_seed }}.
{%- if m.factors %} {{ m.version }} adds training-only augmentation (identifier-prefix randomisation and machine-translated / character-noise copies of training rows); validation and test rows are never augmented.{% endif %}

## Intended and out-of-scope use

Intended: routing short, single-turn logistics chat messages (shipment status, analytics, disruptions, appointments, orders, documents, yard operations, support, knowledge-base, chit-chat) to one of the {{ eda.n_classes }} intents; research and portfolio demonstration of the evaluation methodology.

Out of scope: safety or security controls; regulated or high-stakes decisions; languages other than English, Spanish, French, German and Chinese; messages longer than a short chat turn; relying on the abstention flag to catch new intents (it is a weak detector, see below); any claim of generalisation beyond a {{ eda.n_rows }}-row synthetic dataset.

