## Limitations

- **Weak open-set rejection** (measured): strict rejection recall at 95% retention is {{ tbv.headline.strict_recall_95.point | pct }}% on the headline holdout (CI {{ tbv.headline.strict_recall_95.lo | pct }}% to {{ tbv.headline.strict_recall_95.hi | pct }}%). Do not rely on `abstained` to catch new intents.
- **Identifier-prefix shortcut**: {% if m.shipped %}the shipped model keys on identifier prefixes: the cross-validated neutral-swap flip rate is {{ swap.v1 | f3 }} (the robustness variant v3 reduces it to {{ swap.v3 | f3 }}){% else %}v3 reduces the shortcut but the measurement is limited: the cross-validated neutral-swap flip rate is {{ swap.v3 | f3 }} against {{ swap.v1 | f3 }} for v1 (paired change {{ swap.delta | f3 }}; source `results/phase4e/axes.json`){% endif %}{% if m.test_idswap %}; on the test split the swaps flip {{ m.test_idswap.flip_rate | f3 }} of {{ m.test_idswap.n }} pairs{% if not m.shipped %} (too few pairs to claim the shortcut is gone){% endif %}{% endif %}.
- **Small test set**: n = {{ m.test.n }}; differences between v1 and v3 on Track A are inside the noise.
- **Synthetic data**: {{ eda.n_rows }} synthetic rows from one source; real-world performance is unmeasured.
- **Language coverage**: {{ eda.pct_non_english }}% of messages have a non-English primary language, so non-English behaviour is thinly measured. Under machine translation the prediction agreement with the English prediction is {{ transl.v1 | f3 }} for v1 and {{ transl.v3 | f3 }} for v3 (synthetic translations, not native text).
- **LLM baselines**: only local 8B-class open-weight models ({{ llm_tags | join(', ') }}) were tested; no frontier or hosted LLM was evaluated.

